## Why This Is Asked
Contextual DP problem to test ability to model segmented windows with a non-linear block value (length times max). It also checks precomputation strategy and reconstruction without resorting to brute force.

## Key Concepts
- Interval max precomputation
- Partition DP with exact k segments
- Path reconstruction and complexity trade-offs

## Code Example

```javascript
function solve(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  // precompute maxIn[l][r]
  const maxIn = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let i=0; i<n; i++){
    let m = A[i];
    for (let j=i; j<n; j++){
      m = Math.max(m, A[j]);
      maxIn[i][j] = m;
    }
  }
  // DP arrays would go here (dp and par)
  // Placeholder to illustrate approach
  return null;
}
```

